meta {
  name: Restore decline (return offer)
  type: http
  seq: 13
}

delete {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/master/orders/{{order_id}}/decline
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
  X-Locale: {{locale}}
}

docs {
  # Restore decline — return a declined offer

  Takes this master's decline back: the order shows up again in `available`
  and `by-category`. No push is re-sent.

  The restore window counts from the moment of the decline and is inclusive
  (see `restore_until` in the declined list).

  **Response:** `204 No Content`

  **Errors:**
  - `422` — this master never declined the order, another master already
    took it, it was cancelled, or the restore window is over:
    ```json
    { "message": "Вы не отклоняли эту заявку" }
    { "message": "Заявку уже разобрал другой мастер" }
    { "message": "Заявка больше не доступна" }
    { "message": "Время на возврат отклонённой заявки истекло" }
    ```
  - `403` — the order was declined only by other masters, or the token has
    no usable master profile (see `reason`)
  - `404` — order not found
}
